#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059713 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059526 :question/id #uuid "0adf8fad-9a6f-5eb1-970f-11633ba98ca1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4295" :question/problem "The vectors $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are given in the picture below. Find the coordinates of $\\vec{a}+6\\vec{b}$.\n\n![](images/56/56b10e759084da6fb21c8421bc9ff6d74aac2602df28f6c8e478bd874d7d6e9f.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^(→) + 6b^(→) &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc55e44b-82d0-5145-8a24-d43bc60dc594" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815c3a41-9158-597c-a900-28f71dc19e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3, 5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056527} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c16558-0f65-5213-8725-6982d8f91873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056528} {:answer/id #uuid "2632c7be-399a-59a9-a1c5-d3040176c2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056529} {:answer/id #uuid "3630aa01-0ede-53a0-9581-47ac3d27e799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056530} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7a8a07-59eb-509a-98b9-cc938456eba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056531}] :answer-field/id #uuid "09d60f5c-a8df-5e06-be54-94be00ab60af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056526}] :question/id #uuid "70dfc6f5-0d00-5ccd-bb86-1c88699f5f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-1323" :question/problem "If $u^(→) = ⟨4, 1⟩$ and $v^(→) = ⟨1,-4⟩$, then $u^(→) - v^(→) =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e97a75c-a837-567a-8756-67dfad176334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 11, 4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056605} {:answer/id #uuid "a370905b-4205-5438-b194-1750e2fd465f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 24,-21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056606} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e2d804-4fde-5234-8f14-04d7c065242f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 24, 21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056607} {:answer/id #uuid "f8601e90-71b0-596f-8f7a-24048ce102a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056608} {:answer/id #uuid "66b9ccc9-0bcc-51d3-b695-fcb59bdbbb7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24,-21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056609}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2fd4b126-00ce-5715-a19e-17e93432620d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056604}] :question/id #uuid "a46b9579-0f65-55f3-9e73-31c91369d46c" :question/math-academy-id "q-1386" :question/problem "If $v^(→) = ⟨8,-7⟩$, then $3v^(→) =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233382 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4885183-19e5-5c7a-bc09-9d2bdd330428" :question/math-academy-id "q-1300" :question/problem "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨-3,1⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨4,6⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v}=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v} & =⟨-3,1⟩+⟨4,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3+4,1+6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233395 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c85fb6aa-50dc-5e02-b59e-421805ee7c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-1324" :question/problem "If $\\overset{\\to }{U}=⟨1,3⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{V}=⟨6,3⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{U}+\\overset{\\to }{V}=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{U}+\\overset{\\to }{V} & =⟨1,3⟩+⟨6,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+6,3+3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors Given in Alternative Notation"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059527 :question/id #uuid "e2b211fe-d37a-55dd-bf76-9ffab2b6f128" :question/math-academy-id "e-4297" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -4, 6 \\rangle$. Find $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 36} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048882 :topic/math-academy-id 1101 :topic/title "The Magnitude of a Vector"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "867aed2c-b35e-5007-9ac2-00eb9f789e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056533} {:answer/id #uuid "b570b441-3e76-5296-a70a-898635c0d51b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056534} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5efcaa-fda8-5f46-86a8-ec26f06edd9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056535} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd699d3-7d66-5b5d-9684-70191f970035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056536} {:answer/id #uuid "56b171f0-eae2-5de6-86da-e18b78da9838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056537}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0c808bac-3136-50e9-88db-5847268bcea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056532}] :question/id #uuid "f764385e-ba4e-56aa-912a-4bdb3a698813" :question/math-academy-id "q-1325" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨4,-1⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79d21fc-302a-5450-a54f-6475533b9ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057115} {:answer/id #uuid "e2de1a7d-f3cd-583a-9023-113e1389cccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{152}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057116} {:answer/id #uuid "f12252ac-d673-5896-9285-85965a7929b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057117} {:answer/id #uuid "22c4967f-8145-57dd-b805-7191087f6156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057118} {:answer/id #uuid "3cab3961-9873-5028-99db-92118b7dacac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{157}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057119}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c8bc4442-f564-5392-8824-4c50f5f84d3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057114}] :question/id #uuid "9ada1995-eb39-5223-994f-7ad65f7c8096" :question/math-academy-id "q-18046" :question/problem "Let $a = ⟨ - 12, 3⟩$. Find $\\mid a \\mid$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233594 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8c6e450-fe10-5923-accc-8b824e3c81c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18047" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨5,9⟩.$ Find $|\\,a\\,|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{106}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233595 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26fce79e-92f6-594d-aec2-af45c6145c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18048" :question/problem "if $a=⟨-4,8⟩$, then  what is the magnitude of  $a?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059715 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :question/id #uuid "d4ad6011-24a4-5642-997f-dcc4e807224f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4298" :question/problem "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/f9/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + 3j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j) - (i + 3j) \\\\\n&= i - 5j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050136 :topic/math-academy-id 244 :topic/title "Addition and Scalar Multiplication of Cartesian Vectors in 2D"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa76cd1-659d-5a5b-8d30-aa37db4db6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057121} {:answer/id #uuid "c207c803-b1ce-5924-b942-d55d34b0a896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057122} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4bdbac-dae8-512d-9f28-a6d1ca641844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057123} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31b652-4b6c-5d88-8099-aa3b8dbea173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057124} {:answer/id #uuid "70729c42-11e6-5309-82bb-19226d272451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057125}] :answer-field/id #uuid "21f89363-a985-51cc-946e-14f2aa27f506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057120}] :question/id #uuid "6a56ae9f-24f2-57fe-8fdd-fdcdaeb8e97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18051" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c1f9580f07d06af7ec900ee63c95872e06f459107e64cf1b5117d928efdab22.png)\n\nLet $A(-4, 1)$ and $B(3, 0)$. Find $\\mid AB^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859a4033-c7be-5ff5-af88-1823e959391b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057127} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6482c5-d423-5cfa-b5c4-60571c0a06c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057128} {:answer/id #uuid "e1496379-7a78-53b1-8d89-c51305772b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057129} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ded905-451e-5e8d-87f6-0bff47652269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057130} {:answer/id #uuid "4818a873-c410-58c3-9fa9-c071285aa2cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057131}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60525c6f-c622-5ce0-b076-32a8f28ba4a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057126}] :question/id #uuid "1c261405-1fb7-5f8f-992e-8a8c19696484" :question/math-academy-id "q-18052" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d92a4d7b9c59b0d6bc8ffec9926bcf189c9bbe808c5bed7a02d6ab09bcebcd0.png)\n\nLet $P(-2, 2)$ and $Q(3, 3)$. Find $\\mid PQ^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233366 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02dcce11-c60f-5753-ba12-d8ce046f2ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-125118" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f35a3ad730621023ec86e5727588fc86083ee500b3a72c55ab2808bd290019e9.png)\n\nLet $P(1,2)$ and $Q(-2,1).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+2j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=-2i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+2j) \\\\  & =-3i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233596 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6f7008d-b645-50b0-a00b-9cf227ed2ff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18049" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a250499768a91e3e225a05d141e42d7ed89168ba82c5560777f64b8b29fac4a.png)\n\nLet $C(-1,3)$ and $D(1,-2).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=-i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(i-2j)-(-i+3j) \\\\  & =2i-5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233598 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c14ed0ed-41e3-5534-b77e-503efe93d887" :question/math-academy-id "q-18055" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e3e9c336bf85cf0f19b2326f12c5fd986fee5b0aae65b8d79257ea234efee13.png)\n\nPoints $P$ and $Q$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $P(1,1)$ and $Q(2,3).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=2i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =i+2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :question/id #uuid "65198cdd-dd3b-5840-aaf3-cecd96eb9d3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4301" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 2 \\\\ 0 + (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a + 2b \\mid &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(a + 2b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049360 :topic/math-academy-id 1104 :topic/title "Unit Vectors"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c0ae1f8-a9cf-50fb-bb0e-5bc2b25f22d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057073} {:answer/id #uuid "cc509d88-beba-52ad-90e8-932e39775b94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057074} {:answer/id #uuid "04113066-ce59-5327-a2a0-17fd031b7844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057075} {:answer/id #uuid "3b79648f-cdfe-5e7d-ab62-272eea15302a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057076} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6a7c46-b482-51be-a70e-62fa54b28535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057077}] :answer-field/id #uuid "278a8f50-693e-592e-9524-cda537320d44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057072}] :question/id #uuid "7fcb46f7-1c4e-5d49-b783-5c8f11cf4f94" :question/math-academy-id "q-17709" :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a + 3b$ and points the same direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b3339c8-cfee-5d1c-ad46-ab44efd7b6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057133} {:answer/id #uuid "96688b3e-d471-54f6-8aec-c73d555b7226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057134} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a09e-3906-503f-9e9f-3e6c5b353823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057135} {:answer/id #uuid "29a80b65-88dd-51a4-baa0-c738950c1264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057136} {:answer/id #uuid "401e5f5b-5db4-522a-9b7a-11b15f373032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{76}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{76}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057137}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f8820177-fcee-5d33-9928-79e84e800cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057132}] :question/id #uuid "bfe76e58-e39f-55e9-9d8c-8f6cb0fc0443" :question/math-academy-id "q-18058" :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$ and points the same direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0602d7a4-2911-50a7-8931-1b4bc528c19a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411685} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5b6bc3-0505-592d-8bbe-21764c037dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411711} {:answer/id #uuid "74dbb49a-6f69-59c5-ab9c-6bf2f84350df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411739} {:answer/id #uuid "8c50ba8e-c157-5ca3-9288-576321916d2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411752} {:answer/id #uuid "dda19a54-ac15-5715-b0ab-0a3f1c4ff8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74dbb49a-6f69-59c5-ab9c-6bf2f84350df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411739} :answer-field/id #uuid "760bc6eb-d6bd-5bc8-a1ad-d57d71d59023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411832}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eff15426-c7b2-53a2-8441-6bacd0c6dc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-125135" :question/problem "Let $b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{b}{|b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233368 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06094a0c-ab74-504d-9e7a-29ff1a469a1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125138" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+5 \\\\ 4+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a+b| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(2a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{13} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234271 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af9476c9-5aa2-526b-87d4-a82f7e7eeb39" :question/math-academy-id "q-70409" :question/problem "Let $n=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $n$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|n| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{41}}\\cdot n \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{41}}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{41}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{41}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}]}
